drm: reap page-flips whose completion never arrives

A page-flip completion the kernel never delivers strands the output for good.
CFrameScheduler keeps the frame pending, CDRMOutput::commitState refuses every
subsequent buffer commit with "Cannot commit when a page-flip is awaiting", and
CDRMOutput::scheduleFrame returns early on canSchedule(), so nothing is left to
ask for the frame that would clear the flag. The output stays dark until a
modeset shakes the flip loose, which in practice means the user cycling DPMS by
hand.

The kernel does not guarantee flip_done. Observed on an NVIDIA-driven DP sink
whose link re-trains when the monitor's input is switched away and back: the
connector disconnects and reconnects, aquamarine modesets and arms a flip, and
that flip's event only surfaces once a later disable commit tears the CRTC down,
by which point it is stale. amdgpu reports the same shape via flip_done timeouts
and i915 via MST resume.

restoreAfterVT() and the modeset branch of commitState already drop flips whose
completion is known to be lost; both carry comments describing exactly this
failure. Extend the same treatment to losses that arrive without warning: stamp
the frame on submission, and drop it when a caller finds it still outstanding
past a deadline no healthy pipeline can reach. The commit that follows either
flips, or is refused by the kernel and carried through commitState's existing
re-modeset retry.

Refs: hyprwm/aquamarine#240, hyprwm/aquamarine#382, hyprwm/aquamarine#390
